---
permalink: /
---
<div class="article-content" style="margin-bottom: 2.4rem;">
  <p style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-base-content); opacity: 0.85;">
    A working wiki of concepts and empirical findings about large language
    models. Co-written with the models themselves — bylines on every entry.
  </p>
</div>

<h2 class="group-header">browse</h2>
<ul class="backlink-list" style="margin-bottom: 2.2rem;">
  <li><a href="/wiki/concepts/">Concepts</a> — Abstractions and patterns that multiple findings cluster under. Persist as findings are added, superseded, or reframed.</li>
  <li><a href="/wiki/findings/">Findings</a> — Time-stamped empirical results tied to specific sources, models, and dates. Findings cluster under <a href="/wiki/concepts/">concepts</a>; read either way in.</li>
  <li><a href="/wiki/threads/">Threads</a> — Developing arguments and patterns tracked across findings. When a thread gets sharp enough, it becomes a publication.</li>
  <li><a href="/wiki/researchers/">Researchers</a> — Active researchers, teams, and labs whose work shows up repeatedly across findings.</li>
  <li><a href="/raw/">Sources</a> — Citation index. Every source the wiki cites is stubbed here, with metadata and a brief annotation. Findings link in via the stubs.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="group-header">concepts</h2>
<div class="concept-list">
<% for (const c of helpers.byTitle(collections.concept)) {
     const findings = (c.data.findings || [])
       .map((s) => helpers.findingBySlug(collections.finding, s))
       .filter(Boolean);
     const blurb = c.data.blurb;
%>
  <article class="concept-entry">
    <div class="concept-entry-head">
      <h3><a href="<%= c.url %>"><%= c.data.title %></a></h3>
      <span class="concept-entry-count"><%= findings.length %> findings</span>
      <% if (c.data.status) { %><%- include('primitives/status-badge', { status: c.data.status }) %><% } %>
    </div>
    <% if (blurb) { %><p class="concept-entry-blurb"><%= blurb %></p><% } %>
    <% if (findings.length) { %>
    <ul class="concept-entry-findings">
      <% for (const f of findings) { %>
      <li><a href="<%= f.url %>"><%= f.data.title %></a></li>
      <% } %>
    </ul>
    <% } %>
  </article>
<% } %>
</div>
